## OpenClaw fs-safe Windows move compatibility backport
- Source: https://github.com/openclaw/fs-safe
- Revision: 6ae2e2e5086f2c48b813f78cb65fd787c9879a3f
- Copyright: Copyright (c) 2026 openclaw
- License: MIT License (text below)
- Use: in-memory backport of Windows read-open timestamp handling for the exact fs-safe 0.8.5
  module, with MicroClaw's digest-bound cleanup extension for deferred Windows metadata changes.
  Both move and cleanup modules are source-hash pinned. Installed files are unchanged; path,
  file identity and post-copy checks remain active.

## OpenClaw llama.cpp exact-model setup adapter
- Source: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw
- Package: @openclaw/llama-cpp-provider@2026.9.3
- Use: source-hash-pinned in-memory model-chooser adaptation for Qwen3.5 4B and 9B.
  Adds bounded Windows runtime-directory publication retries after transient locks,
  retaining directory-identity checks and official pre/post-install validation.
  Artifact verification, runtime management and config persistence remain OpenClaw-owned.
  Installed provider files are unchanged.

